:question/id #uuid "9849d588-2a95-5d11-993e-dd1a8d5d4837" :question/math-academy-id "q-129196" :question/problem "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}+z+3?$" :question/worked-solution "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ -{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}+z+3 & =c \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+c-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we let $c-3=C,$ we get a family of elliptic paraboloids:\n\n$$\nz={x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+C,\\,C\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77be6032-ec22-5561-94c2-be289e343142" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Level Surface of a Function Passing Through a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "341c06af-d1ba-5272-bb61-52ad376125d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336522} {:answer/id #uuid "5700ae9e-968d-5bb9-b16c-fb2495caa581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336830} {:answer/id #uuid "726140df-5488-5e91-b878-03e0a7dc18a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337057} {:answer/id #uuid "caa01bba-d8dc-529e-84eb-7a172fdebb43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337815} {:answer/id #uuid "f1709cb8-4e61-5ab7-a2f4-a614c896f494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caa01bba-d8dc-529e-84eb-7a172fdebb43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337815} :answer-field/id #uuid "8165f0ea-43de-5434-a42c-9e10144a7415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e38a7de1-ef3c-50e7-9539-8728abb34f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-71597" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=z-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}$ that passes through the point $P(2,1,22).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1,22) & =22-4(2)^{2}-6(1)^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=0.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ z-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ z & =4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(2,1,22)$ is the elliptic paraboloid $z=4{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}.$"}]}
